From: Cynthia Condra <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep MAXINFO score tables inside long range for large target
 lengths

MaximumInformationTrimmer scales its two log-score tables to long with one
ratio and took Math.max of the two candidate ratios, i.e. the ratio computed
for the table with the smaller maximum. Applied to the length table it pushes
(long) (array[i] * ratio) past Long.MIN_VALUE once targetLength exceeds about
2461 * strictness (248 at 0.1, 495 at 0.2); the saturated value wraps when the
quality sum is added, the first base gets the highest score and every read is
trimmed to one base. From targetLength 711 on Math.exp overflows in the
logistic term and the same happens at every strictness.

Use Math.min so both tables stay inside long range (the quality sum over
LONGEST_READ bases stays below Long.MAX_VALUE / 2), seed calcNormalization
with Math.abs(array[0]), and evaluate log(1/(1+e^x)) as -x for x > 700.
Results at ordinary settings are unchanged.

Adds MaximumInformationTrimmerLargeTargetTest (four tests, three of which
fail without the change).

